From f74871ee014bc5faab2cdf5ff12dd2591912eb3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:10:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] [das] fix(kineto): own roctracer rows with unique_ptr

Why:
RoctracerLogger stores heap-allocated rows as raw pointers and clearLogs() only clears the vector, leaking every captured row on each profiling session; barrier/marker records are also allocated although they are always filtered out.

What:
Store rows as std::unique_ptr, give rocprofBase a virtual destructor, keep a copy of the row in RuntimeActivity instead of a reference, and skip HIP_OP_ID_BARRIER records in the activity callback.

Impact:
Roctracer rows are released by clearLogs(). This patch mirrors the existing third-party ZIP changes.
